{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04VB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$F : \\mathcal{C} \\to S^{-1}\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$S^{-1}\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$F$", "REF_0001": "\\cite[Chapter I, Section 2]{GZ}", "REF_0002": "\\cite[Chapter II, Section 2]{Verdier}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cc435c33ad07fa2a63a7c892e8a9a381aba85f8a43dc6c454651777d2a1a46ed", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3a7664d000f3cc476f7fbb6dd4c0720528a948cc4d209dac2735e572c24851df", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe basic idea of this section is given a category <MATH_0001>\nand a set of arrows <MATH_0002> to construct a functor\n<MATH_0003>\nsuch that all elements of <MATH_0004> become invertible in <MATH_0005>\nand such that <MATH_0006> is universal among all functors with this property.\nReferences for this section are <REF_0001>\nand <REF_0002>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a16d60b6af50c4f8a1a8adc3bb263d2d496ffac723c0599e6cf37ab05dca61a9", "unit_id": "tag:04VB:prose-0001"}
